# Expected skill loads for the screen brief (level: screen, agent: design-builder), derived from the
# Routing table in design-craft/SKILL.md. evals/score.sh reads the first two fields of each line.
#   pass <skill>       a pass row of the part's level for the builder: PASSES needs a result for it.
#                      applied -> its text must come back; n/a -> its text must not come back.
#   must <skill>       a fired trigger or the Verify pass: its text must come back.
#   forbid <skill>     an unfired trigger, a design-only row, another level's row, or a skill out of the router.
#   allow <skill>      may come back; not required.
#   ambiguous <skill>  scored like allow; the routing table leaves the expectation open (see the reason).
# Every skill that comes back and is not pass (applied), must, allow or ambiguous is unexpected.

# The part's level: Screen, flow passes.
pass laws-of-ux                   # row: Screen, flow | Pass: navigation, forms, multi-step flows, destructive actions | both
pass better-interface            # row: Screen, flow | Pass: a review across domains | builder
forbid stageshow                 # row: Screen, flow | Trigger: a product illustration or demo on a page | both (no stage in the fixture)
forbid build-design              # row: Screen, flow | Trigger: a Figma file or a design image is the source | builder (DESIGN.md is the source)

# Verify and Any rows.
must design-qa                   # row: Verify | Pass: every part | both
must browser-checks              # row: Verify | Trigger: any browser step | both (the brief allows a browser)
ambiguous mobile-native            # row: Any | Trigger: phone users | both. DESIGN.md names no phone users (desk office, wall screen, dock-door tablets), but it designs a narrow layout at <= 720px and the brief checks 375 width
forbid copywriting               # row: Any | Trigger: marketing copy | both (app screen, no marketing copy)

# Ambiguous.
ambiguous design-taste-frontend  # row: Product | Pass: which overall look and house rules? | both. Its Notes cell names a "Screen pass for both" (app screen: references/app-screens.md), but the Level cell is Product; index.sh counts a returned read of that reference file as a load
ambiguous interface-review       # row: Component | Pass: the part changed existing UI | builder. The screen changes existing UI (spec D21), but the row is Component level
ambiguous shadcn                 # row: Component | Trigger: the project uses shadcn (components.json) | builder. Fires in this fixture, but the row is Component level and Build step 3 loads the part's level triggers only
forbid ask-sonner                # row: Component | Trigger: toasts with sonner | builder (no sonner in package.json)
forbid coss                      # row: Component | Trigger: the project uses coss or Base UI | builder (components.json style radix-nova; radix-ui, no @base-ui/react)

# Unfired, other-level and design-only rows, and skills out of the router.
forbid better-accessibility        # row: Component | Pass: custom controls, dialogs, focus, keyboard | builder (another level)
forbid better-writing              # row: Component | Pass: labels, errors, empty states, confirmations | builder (another level)
forbid state-machine               # row: Component | Pass: states, one at a time | both (another level)
forbid break-ui                    # row: Component | Pass: renders data: worst-case fixtures and fixes | builder (another level)
forbid review-animations           # row: Component | Pass: changed motion code | builder (another level)
forbid better-colors               # row: Primitive | Pass: palette, semantic tokens, contrast, dark mode | builder (another level)
forbid better-typography           # row: Primitive | Pass: type scale, font loading, wrapping | builder (another level)
forbid better-layout               # row: Primitive | Pass: spacing, grouping, responsive, RTL | builder (another level)
forbid better-ui                   # row: Primitive | Pass: radius, shadow, border, icons | builder (another level)
forbid animate                     # row: Primitive | Pass: motion tokens and new animations | builder (another level)
forbid apple-design              # row: Primitive | Trigger: springs, gestures, drag, sheets | builder (another level)
forbid emil-design-eng           # row: Primitive | Trigger: a motion feel call | builder (another level)
forbid explain-interface         # row: Product | Pass: how was a site the owner names built? | design
forbid find-animation-opportunities # row: Screen, flow | Pass: what here should move? | design
forbid prototype                 # row: Screen, flow | Trigger: a state model or logic question is open | design
forbid improve-animations        # row: Screen, flow | Trigger: the owner asks to improve existing motion | design
forbid variant                   # row: Component | Pass: structure, density, emphasis, type or voice | design
forbid emil-prototype            # row: Component | Pass: motion or interaction feel, while it is open | design
forbid break                     # row: Component | Trigger: every scenario on one page, for one look | design
forbid pick-ui-library           # row: Component | Trigger: a new UI library is needed | design
forbid design-md                 # row: Product | Trigger: the project has no DESIGN.md (create), or the brief calls its direction weak (improve) | design (another agent's row; a builder with no DESIGN.md stops with DECISION NEEDED, D24)
forbid impeccable                # out of router: spec D13
forbid grill-design              # out of router: spec D13
forbid agent-browser             # out of router: spec D13 (the skill stub; the CLI is used directly)
forbid make-interfaces-feel-better # out of router: spec D13
forbid animation-vocabulary      # out of router: spec D13
forbid hallmark                  # out of router: spec D13
forbid coss-particles            # out of router: spec D13
forbid build-design-library      # out of router: spec D4
forbid animate-expo              # out of router: spec D13 platform skill
forbid write-swift               # out of router: spec D13 platform skill
allow design-craft               # injected workflow (agent file inject-skills); a re-read is not a routed load
# Surface recipe (not a skill row, so not scored): the Charts recipe does not fire (no chart on Shipments).
